{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Man vs. Machine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Where Are Things Going?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Explain about technology and technical problems in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Modal Verbs for Speculation", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.</p><p>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Must</span> = it's very likely<br/><span class=\"italic\">Must not</span> / <span class=\"italic\">Could not</span> / <span class=\"italic\">Can't</span> = it's not possible<br/><span class=\"italic\">May</span> / <span class=\"italic\">Might</span> / <span class=\"italic\">Can</span> / <span class=\"italic\">Could</span> = it's possible<br/><span class=\"italic\">May not</span> / <span class=\"italic\">Might not</span> = it's possible this is not true", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He must be at work.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's very likely he's at work.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I can't get her. Her phone must be off.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's likely her phone is off.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They could come over for dinner tomorrow.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Them coming for dinner tomorrow is possible.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They may not come to the movie tonight.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible they are not coming to the movie tonight.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Maps must still be the most common way to find a place.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Cars can have navigational devices that help you find your way.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you're walking, you could ask your cellphone for the directions that you need.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You might have to ask it more than once.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Soon we may be able to get a microchip implanted in our brain.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You put a relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people to make the who you are talking about clearer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things to make the thing  you are talking about clearer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In spoken English and written English, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> often replaces <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>. <span class=\"italic\">Which</span> is generally more formal than <span class=\"italic\">that</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Relative Connector</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Type of Relative Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I stood on a corner talking to the dark rectangle which sat in my hand.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which sat in my hand\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We may be able to get a microchip that will allow us to access the Internet.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that will allow us to access the Internet\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We can access those elusive maps that we need to get around.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that we need to get around\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Ask your cellphone for the directions that you need.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that you need\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "compass", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a device for finding direction", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They invented compasses, then learned to draw accurate maps.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about navigation.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "navigational", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to planning a route", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cars have navigational devices to help you find your way.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "microchip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small electronic device", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Soon we may be able to get a microchip implanted in our brain.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "implant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put into the body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Would you want to have something implanted in your brain?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "elusive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "hard to catch", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He tried to write down that elusive thought he had.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to link", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to connect with", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We might be able to link with Earth's satellites.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "afar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "from a great distance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He admired her from afar.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "probe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a device to look closely at things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We may even connect with a traveling space probe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "marble", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small ball of colored glass", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We could look back at our blue marble from afar.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "unmapped", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unknown; uncharted", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We could turn outward to take in all of unmapped space.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03aud10", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn7le05ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Choose three photos from a magazine, a newspaper or the Internet to write about.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 4 or 5 sentences about each picture.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Speculate about the situation, what is happening and how the people feel.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use complex sentences with who, that or which where possible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Show your pictures to someone and read your sentences to them.  ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write about 3 separate pictures, speculating on the situation, action, and people's feelings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use complex sentences with who, which or that.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my written ideas with another person.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<p>Where are things going?</p>\nIn ancient times, people found their way by looking at the sun and stars. Later, they invented compasses, then learned to draw accurate maps. Maps must still be the most usual way to find a place. However, many people have trouble reading them."}, {"image": "", "time": "17000", "id": 2, "text": "Cars can have navigational devices that help you find your way. If you're walking, you could ask your cellphone for the directions that you need. You might have to ask it more than once. I usually do. Only yesterday I stood on a corner talking to the dark rectangle which sat in my hand. I never found the place that I was looking for."}, {"image": "", "time": "36000", "id": 3, "text": "<p>Soon we may be able to get a microchip implanted in our brain that will allow us to access the Internet and of course those elusive maps that we need to get around.</p>We might link with Earth's satellites to catch the news and views. We may even connect with a traveling space probe to see the blue marble that we live on from afar. Then, we could turn outward to take in all of the unmapped space."}], "video_src": "engenn7le05ob03re2vido1"}, "type": "video"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about technology and gadgets.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can speculate about feelings and impressions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express complex statements using words like <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How easy do you think it is to navigate by the stars?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How do you usually find a new place that you want to go to?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Give me a tall ship and a star to steer her by.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Who lives on the <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_1\">Blue Marble</span>?", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"content": [{"content": "\u201c<span class=\"italic\">The Blue Marble</span>\u201d is a famous photograph of the Earth, taken by the crew of the Apollo 17 in 1972.", "tip_id": 1, "type": "text"}], "type": "tips"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to watch the video.", "type": "text"}],